        <title type="html"><![CDATA[javascript.regular_expressions: duplicate named groups runtime support]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29146</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29146"/>
        <updated>2026-02-27T16:33:25.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2218736?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Add the first versions of Node and Deno that support <a href="https://github.com/tc39/proposal-duplicate-named-capturing-groups">duplicate named capturing groups</a> which appears on <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Regular_expressions/Named_capturing_group#browser_compatibility" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Regular_expressions/Named_capturing_group#browser_compatibility</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>

<p dir="auto">I found the first versions of Node and Deno by explicit testing:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="# Node: unsupported in 22.x, supported in 23.x
npx -y node@22.22.0 -e &quot;try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})-\\d{2}|\\d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(process.version, process.versions.v8);&quot;
npx -y node@23.0.0 -e &quot;try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})-\\d{2}|\\d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(process.version, process.versions.v8);&quot;
# Deno: unsupported in 1.43.6, supported in 1.44.0
npx -y deno@1.46.3 upgrade --version 1.43.6 --output deno1436.exe
./deno1436.exe eval &quot;try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})-\\d{2}|\\d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(Deno.version.deno, Deno.version.v8);&quot;
rm deno1436.exe
npx -y deno@1.46.3 upgrade --version 1.44.0 --output deno1440.exe
./deno1440.exe eval &quot;try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})-\\d{2}|\\d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(Deno.version.deno, Deno.version.v8);&quot;
rm deno1440.exe"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> Node: unsupported in 22.x, supported in 23.x</span>
npx -y node@22.22.0 -e <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})-<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}|<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(process.version, process.versions.v8);<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
npx -y node@23.0.0 -e <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})-<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}|<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(process.version, process.versions.v8);<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
<span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> Deno: unsupported in 1.43.6, supported in 1.44.0</span>
npx -y deno@1.46.3 upgrade --version 1.43.6 --output deno1436.exe
./deno1436.exe <span class="pl-c1">eval</span> <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})-<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}|<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(Deno.version.deno, Deno.version.v8);<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
rm deno1436.exe
npx -y deno@1.46.3 upgrade --version 1.44.0 --output deno1440.exe
./deno1440.exe <span class="pl-c1">eval</span> <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>try { new RegExp('(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})-<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}|<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{2}-(?&lt;year&gt;<span class="pl-cce">\\</span>d{4})'); console.log('supported'); } catch { console.log('unsupported'); } console.log(Deno.version.deno, Deno.version.v8);<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
rm deno1440.exe</pre></div>

<p dir="auto">Node introduced the feature in <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/9d7cd9b864cacb72409e693aa26c36338efa05ca/hovercard" href="https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/9d7cd9b864cacb72409e693aa26c36338efa05ca">nodejs/node@<tt>9d7cd9b</tt></a> (<code class="notranslate">deps: update V8 to 12.8.374.13</code>) which came from <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2433810985" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/54077" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/nodejs/node/pull/54077/hovercard" href="https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/54077">nodejs/node#54077</a> which explicitly lists “RegExp duplicate named capture groups” as a notable change. The commit is mentioned in <a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v23.0.0" rel="nofollow">https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v23.0.0</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Deno introduced this feature in <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/denoland/deno/commit/b009c84bc6f773326d41bbd7f86cec2a5309291a/hovercard" href="https://github.com/denoland/deno/commit/b009c84bc6f773326d41bbd7f86cec2a5309291a">denoland/deno@<tt>b009c84</tt></a> (<code class="notranslate">feat: enable pointer compression via deno_core bump (#23838)</code>) which came from <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2299074801" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/23838" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/denoland/deno/pull/23838/hovercard" href="https://github.com/denoland/deno/pull/23838">denoland/deno#23838</a> which is mentioned in <a href="https://github.com/denoland/deno/releases/tag/v1.44.0">https://github.com/denoland/deno/releases/tag/v1.44.0</a></p>
<p dir="auto">V8 introduced this feature in V8 12.5.x. Relevant commits:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Implement: <code class="notranslate">[regexp] Implement duplicate named capture groups</code>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Gerrit: <a href="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/5200239" rel="nofollow">https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/5200239</a></li>
<li>Commit: <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/f1ad38bed6a36d5f8221d38750ad78e2a8203af3/hovercard" href="https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/f1ad38bed6a36d5f8221d38750ad78e2a8203af3">v8/v8@<tt>f1ad38b</tt></a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Ship: <code class="notranslate">[regexp] Ship duplicate named capture groups</code>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Gerrit: <a href="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/5379754" rel="nofollow">https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/5379754</a></li>
<li>Commit: <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/3ca1bdef7b6f7a75dc7b9e47cf03ebd37861c212/hovercard" href="https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/3ca1bdef7b6f7a75dc7b9e47cf03ebd37861c212">v8/v8@<tt>3ca1bde</tt></a></li>
<li>Moves <code class="notranslate">js_regexp_duplicate_named_groups</code> into shipping features</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
